    <footnotes>
        <footnote id="F1">Reflects the Reporting Person's purchase on November 10, 2026 of 4,546 units from the Issuer, each unit consisting of one share of Common Stock and a warrant to purchase one share of Common Stock (the &quot;PIPE Warrant&quot;), at $5.50 per unit, in a private placement under a Securities Purchase Agreement. No separate consideration was paid for the PIPE Warrant. The closing occurred on November 10, 2026. The PIPE Warrant has an original issue date of November 10, 2026, is exercisable for cash at $10.00 per share, and expires on the fifth anniversary of its original issue date.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F2">Share and underlying-share amounts reflect the 1-for-20 reverse stock split of the Issuer's common stock effective October 12, 2026. The amount beneficially owned following the reported transaction includes 7,833 shares held directly before the transaction, after giving effect to the reverse stock split.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F3">On November 10, 2026, the Reporting Person entered into a Note Amendment and Conversion Agreement with the Issuer that, among other things, reduced the conversion price of his Convertible Promissory Note from $12.00 to $5.50 per share and the exercise price of his Existing Warrant from $16.00 to $13.00 per share. The amendments are reported as the disposition of the original derivative security and the acquisition of the amended derivative security. The original securities are treated as disposed of solely for purposes of this Form 4 reporting; they were amended and remain outstanding as amended. The transactions were approved in advance by the Issuer's Board of Directors on November 10, 2026 for purposes of Rule 16b-3(d) and (e). Share amounts reflect the 1-for-20 reverse stock split effective October 12, 2026. The original Note and Existing Warrant were issued on April 17, 2026.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F4">The conversion price is subject to reset on the first anniversary of issuance and at maturity. The Note converts at the Issuer's closing of the contemplated merger or earlier at the holder's election, subject to the Exchange Cap.</footnote>
    </footnotes>

